{"c":[{"id":"d9542f01119cf37d","sum":"B19-B20: undoing a skill run resets its clean count. A listen-only tap per pid sees clicks posted to that pid (global monitor and session tap do not); a background-only caret-fixture takes no posted click, --foreground (accessory) does.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T221243Z-e77935deee83e487","text":"Skills (B19): undoing a skill run resets its clean count, so a fixture forced-mismatch run with no Tab needs ten more clean runs after run 11's undo. Live Jev's first naming ask fell under NAME_CUTOFF 0.5 in 7 of 9 tries; the reworded retry picked.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T234914Z-795f3dcc958c0f2c","text":"A listen-only tap per pid sees clicks posted to that pid; the global NSEvent monitor and a session tap do not (B20, 6 of 6 vs 0 of 6). A background-only caret-fixture takes no posted click and cannot hit-test a covered window; --foreground (accessory) does both.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e619089820dda277","sum":"B20: input posted to a pid resets HIDIdleTime like a person's, so GUI evals record their last post (scripts/synthetic-input.ts) or the idle gate stops them. TextEdit cannot host a routine: one text area, no positions, one value per field.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T234914Z-993bc2a42fa75599","text":"Input posted to a pid (CGEventPostToPid) resets HIDIdleTime like a person's (B20: 196 s to 0.3 s); GUI evals that post input record their last post (helper/scripts/synthetic-input.ts) or the idle gate stops them as 'user back'.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T234914Z-ac2ee9392ce81473","text":"TextEdit cannot host a B19 routine: a shape is (source template, part, destination template) with no positions, a document is one text area, values copied from list lines share one source template, and engine.plan writes one value per field (B20).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
